//  6. The "has direction" flag at +0x10 of a 0x18 directed-friction record
//     is a UBYTE (stb) — m2c wrote s32/stw. The +0x20 flag of a 0x28
//     constraint record IS s32/stw.
//  7. *(f32 *)0x80298Dxx -> `extern f32 lbl_80298Dxx;` plain reads. want uses
//     the two-word `lis @ha` + `lfs @l` symbol form with a SEPARATE anchor
//     per symbol (0x800B821C/0x800B8220), which a bare literal cannot make.
//  8. fn_80271070/fn_80271170 (cosf/sinf) are f32-RETURNING; m2c used the
