//     (95 f32 slots), ONE saved FPR (f31) and stmw r21; got `stwu -0xE8`
//     with 9 saved FPRs and stmw r17. This is DOWNSTREAM of A-D: the 95
//     declared f32 locals only occupy slots while something reads or
//     writes them, so the dead ones are dropped and the frame collapses.
//     Fixing the frame without A-D is not possible without asm, and asm
//     is banned for this work.
//
// RETRY HINTS (in order of value):
//  1. Decode the primary-opcode-4 words with a CORRECTED psq/op4 decoder
//     before touching this fn again. `tools/ps_disasm.py` and capstone
//     BOTH mis-decode here: the psq base register is bits 20..16
//     (OPC(6) | rt(5) | ra(5) | W(1) | I(3) | d(12), d in BYTES), NOT
//     w&0x1f, and the d field is what `psq` prints as a decimal. Getting
//     this wrong made the whole first pass read arg1 as the psq base
//     instead of arg0. Also: capstone and ps_disasm label plain Gekko
//     paired-single as AltiVec/VMX, and the xo10=6/7 words here
//     (0x10000318 etc.) are NOT a hard wall — see AGENTS.md §6ax-218 /
//     §6ai-152, they are emittable `__ps_t`/builtin forms under
